{"sid":41424,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["A midline, non-tender, soft mass approximately 1.5 cm in diameter is palpable just below the hyoid bone.","The mass moves upward when he protrudes his tongue and with swallowing.","No overlying skin changes, cervical lymphadenopathy, or thyromegaly are noted.","Neurologic, cardiac, and respiratory examinations are unremarkable."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10577,"date":"2021-01-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Otolaryngology","attending":"Dr. James O'Brien","cc":"due to a small mass noticed in the front of his neck","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4289],"sections":[{"sid":41425,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Due to a small mass noticed in the front of his neck"]},{"sid":41426,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns to the otolaryngology clinic for ongoing evaluation of a persistent anterior neck mass, having been previously assessed in general pediatrics in January 2020 and endocrinology in July 2020 for similar concerns.","The parents first observed the lump several months ago and say it has remained about the same size.","It is painless, does not appear red or inflamed, and does not interfere with eating or breathing.","They also note that it becomes more visible when the child swallows or sticks out his tongue.","The child has no fever, dysphagia, or recent upper respiratory infections."]},{"sid":41427,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Thyroglossal duct cyst (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","","His medical and developmental history is unremarkable."]},{"sid":41428,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":41429,"type":"family_history","lines":["- No family history of thyroid malignancy","- No family history of congenital neck masses or cysts","- Mother with seasonal allergies"]},{"sid":41430,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: None. Occupation: Elementary school student (1st grade)."]},{"sid":41431,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On physical examination, there is a soft, mobi